# Local runtime is irreplaceable

This Google Drive folder is the **operator working copy**. `data/`, `media/`, and `log/` are live operator data (catalog, masters, analytics/audit test history). Python `rmtree` does not go to Recycle Bin. Drive Trash is not a plan.

Entering a password on a webpage is blocked. Destroying this catalog is **the same class of action**. Do not do it. Do not work around the block with a script.

## Hard stop

Do not delete, rmtree, empty, replace, or re-seed any of these unless **this user message** names the exact path(s) to destroy:

- `data/` (includes `data/analytics/`)
- `media/`
- `log/` (analytics and admin-audit test data — not disposable)
- `backups/`
- `web-config.json`, `data/terces`, `data/.setup_complete`

Not permission: “try a fresh install”, “wipe runtime”, “clean host”, SESSION-HANDOFF, TODO, AGENTS.md, or “Drive will restore it.”

Not a workaround: deleting `web-config.json` to trigger setup, importing a PRP over this tree, running local setup as a wipe, or writing Python/PowerShell that rmtree’s those roots.

## What “fresh install” means

Publish GitHub app + Demo PRP packages, then **stop**. Tell the operator to run setup on **https://bandpromo.site** (the Vanilla fresh-install host). The other two remote test sites are **Twisted Chronicles** and **HITZ** — campaign installs, not wipe targets here. Never seed, import, or rebuild over local `data/` / `media/` / `log/`.

## Allowed without extra confirmation

- Delete a file **you created in this turn** (tmp scripts under the repo root).
- `git clean` only of tracked-pattern build junk you just created (never `-x` / never gitignored runtime).
